        "original_id": "1a1ddac2-b51e-54c7-b429-187bb780fd7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacky Ickx, Pedro Rodríguez\n- Organizations: BRM, Ferrari, WilliamsF1\n- Events: 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, 1979 Can-Am season, 24 Hours of Le Mans, Dakar Rally\n- Products: Williams FW31\n- Topics: Formula One, Can-Am Championship\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Pedro Rodríguez finished second for BRM.\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Ferrari driver Jacky Ickx finished third.\n- Jacky Ickx was born on 1 January 1945 in Brussels and is a Belgian former racing driver.\n- Jacky Ickx won the 24 Hours of Le Mans six times.\n- Jacky Ickx achieved eight Formula One wins and 25 Formula One podium finishes.\n- In the 1979 Can-Am season, Jacky Ickx was declared champion.\n- In the 1979 Can-Am season, Jacky Ickx won five of the ten rounds and finished second at Road Atlanta.\n- Jacky Ickx is a former winner of the Dakar Rally.\n- The Williams FW31 is a Formula One motor racing car designed and built by WilliamsF1.",
